w"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>57149244</doc-number><kind>U</kind></document-id><sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-60089143-U" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>60089143</doc-number><kind>U</kind></document-id><sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1162152A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HAGIHARA TADASHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HAGIHARA, TADASHI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HAGIHARA TADASHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HAGIHARA, TADASHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A self-standing bag vacuum container having a wall surface formed of a soft sheet and provided with a self-standing container, a spout and a check valve provided to the spout, characterized in that the check valve, on receiving a spouting-direction pressure, allows the contained substance to move and, on receiving a filling-direction pressure, closes, whereby keeping the inside of the container vacuum. The stand pouch-like self-standing vacuum container constructed as above is suitable for preserving a beverage or the like which is likely to be oxidized when in contact with air and is therefore aerophobic, and can sustain itself firmly in spite of its reduced contents.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention se rapporte à un contenant à vide de type sac autoportant qui présente une surface de paroi formée d'une feuille souple, un bec verseur et un clapet de non-retour disposé sur ledit bec verseur. Ce contenant se caractérise en ce que, lorsqu'une pression est appliquée sur le clapet de non retour dans le sens permettant l'écoulement du contenu par le bec verseur, ledit clapet permet l'écoulement dudit contenu et, lorsqu'une pression y est appliquée dans le sens permettant le remplissage du contenant, le clapet de non-retour se ferme, ce qui permet de maintenir l'intérieur du contenant vide. Le contenant à vide de type sac autoportant de cette invention permet de conserver une boisson ou analogue qui est susceptible de s'oxyder au contact de l'air et qui ne supporte donc pas le contact avec l'air. Ce contenant présente l'avantage de pouvoir tenir en position verticale même lorsque son contenu est réduit.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>